    fix(node): refuse an unusable deploy key before spawning (CF-003)
    
    node-create.sh --deploy-key validated only that the file was readable and mode
    600/400. A mode-600 `.pub`, a non-key file, a passphrase-protected key and an
    HTTPS (or local-path) remote all passed that gate, so an agent was spawned and
    the key bytes were copied into it before deploy_key.py refused them INSIDE the
    node — exactly the clone failure 40 seconds later that the preflight comment
    claims to prevent. Measured at 4f32a50: each of the four printed
    `PASS deploy_key — … mode 600` and went on to spawn.
    
    The spawn gate now asks ssh-keygen (the client that will present the key) to
    load it, and refuses the remote forms a deploy key cannot authenticate, so the
    refusal lands on the control host before an agent exists:
      FAIL deploy_key:loadable — <path> does not load as an unencrypted private key
      FAIL deploy_key:repo     — <url> is not an SSH remote / is a local path
    An unreadable key, a 0644 key and `--deploy-key` with no --repo keep their named
    refusals. The exact SSH form stays deploy_key.py install's job, so a form the
    gate does not recognise gets no row rather than a PASS it did not measure.
    
    tests/selftest.sh section 58 gains six arms on a real ssh-keygen fixture:
    public key, junk file and encrypted key refused at the gate, an HTTPS remote
    refused, a green control (a usable key passes both rows and the run continues to
    server_declared, so "refuses everything" cannot read as a pass), and a red proof
    that pre-fix 4f32a50 accepted the public key. Section 58 also points its
    ch:trace spec= at specs/NODE.md#credentials--per-repo-deploy-keys instead of an
    OUTLINE anchor that does not resolve.
    
    Verification: python3 tests/test_node_provisioning.py -> Ran 23 tests, OK;
    bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (429 PASS rows, 61 FAIL rows echoed by
    arms that assert a refusal, 0 SKIP); bash scripts/boardctl validate ->
    RESULT: OK (7 pre-existing warnings); gitleaks detect --no-git -> no leaks found.
    
    Still open and NOT claimed (no live host exercised here): cloning the real
    private GitLab from a fresh node with a real read-only key, the 11 node-dependent
    Go tests / suite 30/30 on a clean node, the 656 MB cache saving measured against
    a live node, a live footprint admission, and reaping a live host's orphans.
    
